# Shemá — the two people directories (BE-13 · OBT-402)
#
# The org chart and the intercessor network. They are two directories of human
# beings and deliberately not one model: docs/shema.md §5.7 forbids a reference
# between them in either direction, so the network is never joined to a role and
# a seat never points at a network contact.
#
# Read access is narrower than authentication, and the rule is:
#   GET /regions                    any Shemá member — the organisation's own
#                                   directory of offices, names only, no contact
#   /regions/role-changes           coordinator, and only their regions
#   /regions/{key}/team (GET, PUT)  coordinator, and only their region
#   everything under /prayer/...    resourceCircle, and nobody else
#
# Before running: seed the app and its roles, then grant. An account may hold
# more than one Shemá role and here it needs two, because the two directories
# answer to two different roles.
#   uv run python scripts/seed_apps_roles.py
#   uv run python scripts/grant_app_role.py shema.local@test.com shema coordinator
# The region scope is the module's own table and has no route yet:
#   app/services/shema/set_region_scope.py, called by an operator.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@accessToken = PASTE_FROM_AUTH_LOGIN

### The chart — seven regions, three seats each, assigned or not
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/regions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### One region's seats, with the account behind each — what the editor loads
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/regions/asia/team
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Put three names in three seats. A seat left empty is a seat cleared.
# The answer is {outcome: {changed, filled, cleared}, changes: RoleChange[]} —
# a save that changed nothing says so, which a 204 could not carry.
# `accounts` is optional and per seat; an account sent beside a new name belongs
# to the new holder, and a name change with no account beside it clears the old.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/regions/asia/team
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "team": {"coordinator": "Ana Lima", "obtLab": "Bruno Sá", "resourceCircle": ""},
  "accounts": {"coordinator": "PASTE_A_REAL_USER_ID"}
}

### The audit trail — the one surface that shows somebody who left a seat
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/regions/role-changes
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

# --- the network. resourceCircle only, from here down. ------------------------

### The directory — everyone who consented to be listed
# No contact string anywhere in the body: contactChannel and contactHint say how
# somebody is reached and which of two people with one name this is, and are
# worth nothing in bulk. withheldCount is how many the consent gate removed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/intercessors
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Add a contact — the basis is required, and the two rows are one transaction
# A person cannot be stored without a recorded basis. docs/shema.md §10 item 8
# asks what consent was given and how it is evidenced; this is where it lands.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/intercessors
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Maria Santos",
  "country": "BR",
  "contact": "maria.santos@example.org",
  "sensitiveCountry": false,
  "consentBasis": "verbal, at the 2026 regional gathering"
}

### Consent to being listed internally — which is not consent to an export
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/intercessors/PASTE_ID/consents/directory
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"basis": "asked on the call of 3 March, said yes to the internal list"}

### Consent to appearing in something that leaves the organisation
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/intercessors/PASTE_ID/consents/partner-export
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"basis": "signed form on file, 2026-04-02"}

### Withdraw one consent — the row is deleted, never flagged
# Withdrawing `network` erases the person: it was the basis the row existed on.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/intercessors/PASTE_ID/consents/directory
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### One contact, for one person. The server logs the read.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/intercessors/PASTE_ID/contact
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Edit. addedAt has no field here and survives.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/intercessors/PASTE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"contact": "+55 11 98765-4321"}

### Erase — the row and its consents leave storage. No tombstone.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/intercessors/PASTE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
